      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I had an LG RESU10H battery, Sunny Boy Storage 2.5 and Sunny Tripower 20000TL-30 inverter installed by Inspire Energy in early 2018 and it has generally worked OK, but it has never worked to provide backup power in cases of a grid outage. I repeatedly chased Inspire Energy to resolve but was eventually told by them that it was incorrectly designed, and I would have to spend several thousand dollars to upgrade it to provide the functionality they promised originally.I discovered my battery was subject to recall when I saw an ACCC advertisement - I was never contacted by LG or Inspire. I have now been waiting for action on the recall process since October 2021, after reaching out to LG directly.I followed up repeatedly with LG directly, the recall team, and Inspire Energy. I was given a wide range of different stories and no timeframe for resolution, until finally in early December 2022 I was given a date for the replacement to take place.Inspire Energy stopped responding both to myself and LG and would not perform the replacement.At the end of December, another team engaged by LG, the Solar Service Guys, arrived and replaced the battery but could not get the new battery to work correctly. I have had to follow up myself several times as they will not return phone calls or send promised emails.Customer service from both Inspire Energy and LG has been nothing short of appalling. I would strongly urge you to avoid dealing with either of them in any form, I certainly won't be again.",
